# v38 OVERLAY (user 2026-11-03, after v37 was stopped at 216k): v30's reward
# and the user's 200 m goal chaining, WITHOUT the throttle floor.
#
# WHY THE FLOOR IS GONE. v37 was v30 + chaining + MIN_THROTTLE=0.15 and ran
# behind v30 at every matched step (policy 0.030 vs 0.150 at 200k) on the same
# eval set: 11.9 m driven per episode against 34.5 m, 47 steps against 113,
# and 36 of 40 episodes ending off-road or in a collision against v30's 18
# off-road / 18 crossing / 4 reached. Collisions went from about 0 to 8 per 40,
# which is what a car that cannot brake does. The floor was the only change
# touching every step -- chaining, GOAL_KEEP_ON_PASS, the value ceiling and the
# stall net are all inert at a 0.05 goal rate -- so it carries the difference.
#
# The dead zone below 0.14 throttle is real (scripts/throttle_probe.py), but
# the damage it does is the ABSORBING TRAP: an episode spent stationary for the
# whole clock. STALL_TRUNCATE_STEPS ends those in 5 s and leaves the car able
# to slow and stop, which v30 evidently used. v30 itself never stalled once in
# 140 eval episodes, so a policy trained this way does not need the floor.
. "$REPO/slurm/v30_overlay.env"

# -- the user's chaining: a new goal 10-30 m past the next junction on each
# arrival, until 200 m is driven. A chain continuation stays a GOAL episode
# (gated_reward.reset), or half of them would land in the explore arm.
export GOAL_CHAIN_M=200 GOAL_CHAIN_MIN_M=10 GOAL_CHAIN_MAX_M=30 GOAL_CHAIN_LOOKAHEAD_M=60
# The env must not move the goal on a too-fast pass: the goal image is latched
# at reset, so a resample there leaves the planner and the image disagreeing.
export GOAL_KEEP_ON_PASS=1

# -- the stall net alone (no MIN_THROTTLE): 100 steps (5 s) under 0.5 km/h
# truncates, so a car in the dead zone loses 5 s instead of the whole episode.
export STALL_TRUNCATE_STEPS=100 STALL_SPEED_KMH=0.5

# NOT SET, deliberately, so this differs from v30 only by the chaining and the
# stall net: MIN_THROTTLE (v37's floor) and TQC_VALUE_CEILING (v30 runs the
# 150 default; a chained leg pays at most ~30 m of route progress plus the 100
# arrival, so 150 is not binding).

# -- v30's launch settings, which v30 passed on the command line.
export HER=1 REPLAY_CAPACITY=1000000 REPLAY_DEVICE=cpu REPLAY_U8=1
export DET_EPISODE_FRAC=0.15 VIDEO_EVERY=20
